0
00:00:01,134 --> 00:00:04,738
Tyra:
PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

1
00:00:04,738 --> 00:00:07,374
THE GIRLS NOT ONLY LEARNED ABOUT
PARISIAN HAUTE COUTURE.

2
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:10,477
THEY LEARNED ABOUT PARISIAN MEN.

3
00:00:10,477 --> 00:00:11,345
Shannon: SO THIS IS OUR DINNER?

4
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:12,479
Man: THIS IS IT.

5
00:00:12,479 --> 00:00:14,281
Adrianne: OKAY.

6
00:00:14,281 --> 00:00:17,217
Tyra: A NUDE PHOTO SHOOT PUSHED
SOME GIRLS TO THEIR LIMITS.

7
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:20,454
Robin: THIS WEEK, IT'S TWO
STRANDS OF RIBBON AND A THONG.

8
00:00:20,454 --> 00:00:22,723
WHAT IS IT GONNA BE NEXT WEEK?

9
00:00:22,723 --> 00:00:25,659
Tyra: AND ROBIN WAS THE ONE
ASKED TO LEAVE.

10
00:00:28,495 --> 00:00:31,164
NOW ONLY THREE GIRLS REMAIN:

11
00:00:31,164 --> 00:00:33,567
SHANNON, THE ALL-AMERICAN
VIRGIN.

12
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:35,235
Shannon: I'VE GOT WHAT IT TAKES.

13
00:00:35,235 --> 00:00:40,707
Tyra: ELYSE, THE HIGH-FASHION,
PRE-MED STUDENT.

14
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:45,379
AND ADRIANNE,
THE ROCK-N-ROLL TOMBOY.

15
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:48,148
Adrianne: PLUS, I'M FUNNY,
I'M PRETTY.

16
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:50,417
I GOT PERFECT TEETH.

17
00:00:50,417 --> 00:00:54,621
Tyra: ONE OF THESE GIRLS WILL BE
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

18
00:00:54,621 --> 00:01:18,045
♪♪♪

19
00:01:41,368 --> 00:01:44,237
Elyse: I MISS ROBIN.

20
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:47,407
(Adrianne laughing)

21
00:01:47,407 --> 00:01:49,042
Adrianne: THAT WAS FUNNY.

22
00:01:49,276 --> 00:01:51,478
I'M REALLY HAPPY ROBIN'S GONE.

23
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:53,080
I'M GONNA BE ABLE TO DO
WHAT I WANT

24
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,748
AND NOT GET
IN TROUBLE FOR IT.

25
00:01:54,748 --> 00:01:57,050
HOW DO YOU LIKE
THESE APPLES, BABY?

26
00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:58,151
HOW DO YOU LIKE 'EM?

27
00:01:58,151 --> 00:01:59,319
HOW DO YOU LIKE 'EM?

28
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,721
HOW DO YOU LIKE 'EM?
Shannon: OH, MY GOSH!

29
00:02:00,721 --> 00:02:02,723
Elyse: ADRIANNE, SHANNON AND
MYSELF LIVING IN THE HOUSE,

30
00:02:02,723 --> 00:02:05,225
I THINK WILL BE PRETTY PLEASANT.

31
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:06,727
IT'D BE NICE TO SEE MORE OF
SHANNON'S TRUE COLORS

32
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:08,662
AND SEE HER LET
LOOSE A LITTLE BIT,

33
00:02:08,662 --> 00:02:10,564
WHICH I DON'T THINK SHE DID
AROUND ROBIN.

34
00:02:10,564 --> 00:02:12,065
Elyse: DO THE STOMP, GIRL.

35
00:02:12,065 --> 00:02:14,334
PUT YOUR MONEYMAKER TO WORK.

36
00:02:14,334 --> 00:02:16,036
Adrianne: MY MONEYMAKER.

37
00:02:16,036 --> 00:02:17,337
Shannon: I DO MISS ROBIN.

38
00:02:17,337 --> 00:02:19,306
SHE WAS, LIKE, SORT OF LIKE MY
MOTHER IN THE HOUSE,

39
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:21,975
BUT I DO FEEL COMFORTABLE WITH
ELYSE AND ADRIANNE.

40
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:24,411
THEY'RE FUN, AND AT LEAST NOW I
CAN BE MORE OUTGOING IN A WAY,

41
00:02:24,411 --> 00:02:27,080
AND I DON'T HAVE TO WORRY ABOUT
LIKE, BEING QUIET ALL THE TIME,

42
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:30,283
'CAUSE I-- THAT IN A WAY, I WAS
LIKE THAT A LITTLE BIT,

43
00:02:30,283 --> 00:02:31,618
MAYBE WHEN SHE WAS AROUND.

44
00:02:31,618 --> 00:02:37,557
♪♪

45
00:02:37,557 --> 00:02:41,128
Shannon: I CAN'T BELIEVE THAT
I'M IN THE FINAL THREE.

46
00:02:41,128 --> 00:02:43,130
Adrianne: AND ALL THOSE PEOPLE
THAT TOLD ME THAT

47
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,531
I WASN'T GONNA MAKE IT TO THE
END CAN JUST...

48
00:02:44,531 --> 00:02:47,668
BECAUSE I'M STILL HERE.

49
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:48,268
Shannon: YEAH, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO THINK.

50
00:02:48,268 --> 00:02:50,137
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

51
00:02:50,137 --> 00:02:52,439
'CAUSE WE'RE ALL, LIKE, BLONDE
HAIR, SHORT HAIR, BROWN HAIR.

52
00:02:52,439 --> 00:02:54,007
Elyse: THE THREE OF US ARE HERE.

53
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:56,276
I CAN'T EVEN SPECULATE AS TO
WHO'S GONNA BE ELIMINATED.

54
00:02:56,276 --> 00:02:58,111
WE'LL JUST HAVE TO SEE WHAT WE
HAVE TO DO.

55
00:02:58,111 --> 00:02:59,212
Tyra: HELLO.
Adrianne: HI.

56
00:02:59,212 --> 00:03:00,480
Shannon: HEY!
Elyse: HI.

57
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:03,717
Tyra: WHY IS EVERYBODY MATCHING,
LIKE RED AND ORANGE?

58
00:03:03,717 --> 00:03:05,052
SO, Y'ALL, IT'S GETTING DOWN TO
THE WIRE.

59
00:03:05,052 --> 00:03:06,319
Shannon: I KNOW!

60
00:03:06,319 --> 00:03:07,487
Tyra: WHAT YOU GUYS ARE ABOUT TO
EXPERIENCE RIGHT NOW

61
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:09,556
IS THE PINNACLE OF AMERICAN
FASHION.

62
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:12,092
YOU'VE ALREADY EXPERIENCED THE
PINNACLE OF FRENCH FASHION,

63
00:03:12,092 --> 00:03:16,997
WHICH IS HAUTE COUTURE, BUT NEW
YORK FASHION WEEK IS THE TOP,

64
00:03:16,997 --> 00:03:19,766
THE MOST AMAZING THING ABOUT
AMERICAN FASHION.

65
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:21,468
AND WE'RE GONNA SEE IF YOU GUYS

66
00:03:21,468 --> 00:03:25,205
HAVE WHAT IT TAKES
TO BE IN A FASHION SHOW.

67
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:26,606
Shannon: WOW.

68
00:03:26,606 --> 00:03:28,141
Tyra: I'M GONNA HAVE YOU MEET
DREW LINEHAN,

69
00:03:28,141 --> 00:03:30,410
WHO'S A FASHION SHOW PRODUCER
HERE IN NEW YORK,

70
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:33,146
AND HE'S GONNA TELL YOU ALL
ABOUT FASHION WEEK.

71
00:03:33,146 --> 00:03:34,014
Y'ALL READY?

72
00:03:34,014 --> 00:03:35,348
YES.

73
00:03:35,348 --> 00:03:39,553
♪♪

74
00:03:46,626 --> 00:03:47,994
Drew: I'M DREW.
I'M SHANNON.

75
00:03:47,994 --> 00:03:49,663
SHANNON, HOW ARE YOU?

76
00:03:49,663 --> 00:03:52,566
ELYSE, NICE TO MEET YOU.
ADRIANNE, NICE TO MEET YOU.

77
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:55,102
I PRODUCE AND CAST FASHION SHOWS
DURING FASHION WEEK.

78
00:03:55,102 --> 00:03:57,704
IT'S A REALLY, REALLY IMPORTANT
TIME FOR YOUR CAREER.

79
00:03:57,704 --> 00:04:00,540
WHEN YOU GO TO THESE SHOWS,
THE PEOPLE IN THE FRONT ROW

80
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:03,176
ARE THE MOST
IMPORTANT PEOPLE IN FASHION.

81
00:04:03,176 --> 00:04:06,079
IT IS A GRUELING THREE WEEKS.

82
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:08,281
YOUR HAIR IS BEING RIPPED OUT.

83
00:04:08,281 --> 00:04:11,051
YOUR FEET ARE BEING SHOVED IN
SHOES THAT DON'T FIT.

84
00:04:11,051 --> 00:04:12,219
IT'S TOUGH.

85
00:04:12,219 --> 00:04:15,055
WHEN YOU GO ON A GO SEE,
IT'S A JOB INTERVIEW.

86
00:04:15,055 --> 00:04:17,991
YOU ARE TRYING
TO WIN THE JOB FROM ME.

87
00:04:17,991 --> 00:04:20,160
YOU HAVE TO, LIKE, YOU KNOW,
WORK THE CLIENT...

88
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:23,296
Elyse: WHEN DREW WAS GIVING HIS
BIG LECTURE,

89
00:04:23,296 --> 00:04:25,165
IT WAS REALLY BORING, AND IT WAS
HARD TO PAY ATTENTION,

90
00:04:25,165 --> 00:04:27,434
AND MY EYES WERE GLAZING OVER.

91
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:29,703
ONE GIRL WAS SORT
OF DOZING OFF, YOU KNOW?

92
00:04:29,703 --> 00:04:31,505
YOU CAN'T DOZE OFF.

93
00:04:31,505 --> 00:04:33,573
I MEAN,
YOU'RE HERE TO SELL YOURSELF.

94
00:04:33,573 --> 00:04:37,611
MAKE SURE YOU SAY, "GOODBYE,"
"THANK YOU" AND "SEE YOU AGAIN."

95
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,645
NICE MEETING YOU ALL.

96
00:04:38,645 --> 00:04:40,447
GOOD LUCK WITH EVERYTHING.

97
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:41,748
Shannon: THANK YOU,
HAD FUN, THANKS.

98
00:04:41,748 --> 00:04:42,716
Drew: THANK YOU VERY MUCH,
NICE MEETING YOU.

99
00:04:42,716 --> 00:04:44,217
Adrianne: VERY NICE MEETING YOU.

100
00:04:44,217 --> 00:04:45,252
Shannon: AND I WILL SEE YOU
AGAIN.

101
00:04:45,252 --> 00:04:46,319
Drew: EXACTLY,
GOOD FOR YOU.

102
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,161
Adrianne: I JUST FEEL LIKE

103
00:04:54,161 --> 00:04:57,998
THROWING YOU AROUND LIKE
A RAG DOLL.

104
00:04:57,998 --> 00:05:00,033
Elyse: WHAT ARE WE DOING?

105
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:01,701
Adrianne: HAVING OUR TALK
WITH SHANNON.

106
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:03,537
Elyse: SHANNON, WHEN A MAN AND A
WOMAN

107
00:05:03,537 --> 00:05:06,106
LOVE EACH OTHER VERY MUCH, LIKE
YOUR FATHER AND I...

108
00:05:06,106 --> 00:05:10,043
Shannon: NO!

109
00:05:10,043 --> 00:05:11,545
DO YOU WANT ME TO TEACH
YOU A SELF-DEFENSE MOVE?

110
00:05:11,545 --> 00:05:12,345
Adrianne: SURE.

111
00:05:12,345 --> 00:05:14,181
HEY, BABY!

112
00:05:14,181 --> 00:05:16,149
LIKE HE'S DRUNK AND TRYING TO
PUT HIS ARM AROUND ME LIKE THIS.

113
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:17,417
I GO LIKE THIS.

114
00:05:17,417 --> 00:05:18,451
WAIT, DON'T DO THAT.

115
00:05:18,451 --> 00:05:20,020
Adrianne: YOUR FINGER IS IN MY
FINGERS.

116
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:21,655
Shannon: AND I'M LIKE THIS
AND I'M LIKE THIS.

117
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:22,756
OW, THAT HURTS.

118
00:05:22,756 --> 00:05:24,424
OH, YEAH, BABY!

119
00:05:24,424 --> 00:05:26,626
Elyse: THE MORE I GET TO KNOW
SHANNON, THE MORE I LIKE HER.

120
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:28,995
I THINK SHE'S REALLY, REALLY
GENUINE.

121
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:32,299
Adrianne: AND I REALLY ENJOYED
OUR PAST COUPLE OF DAYS TOGETHER

122
00:05:32,299 --> 00:05:34,634
BECAUSE MY EVIL INFLUENCE

123
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:36,703
HAS BROUGHT OUT THE WORST
IN SHANNON.

124
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:37,971
Adrianne: STOP!

125
00:05:37,971 --> 00:05:39,539
SHANNON!

126
00:05:39,539 --> 00:05:42,342
(laughing)

127
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:44,544
Shannon: I THINK I'M MORE MYSELF
NOW BECAUSE

128
00:05:44,544 --> 00:05:48,615
I CAN AT LEAST, UM, BE SORT OF
SILLY AT TIMES.

129
00:05:51,484 --> 00:05:53,186
YOU CAN'T GET ME WHEN I'M
ALREADY DOWN!

130
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:57,724
♪♪

131
00:05:57,724 --> 00:05:59,759
Shannon: OH, I LIKE THIS HAT.

132
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:01,161
THE LAST COUPLE OF DAYS WE'VE
HAD SOME FREE TIME,

133
00:06:01,161 --> 00:06:03,463
SO WE'VE BEEN OUT IN NEW YORK
SHOPPING AROUND.

134
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:05,298
Shannon: OH, MY WORD,
THIS IS SO COOL.

135
00:06:05,298 --> 00:06:07,701
OH, MY WORD!

136
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:09,069
I DON'T FEEL
LIKE I'M THE THIRD WHEEL.

137
00:06:09,069 --> 00:06:10,437
NORMALLY, WHEN YOU HAVE THREE
TOGETHER,

138
00:06:10,437 --> 00:06:13,073
ONE FEELS, LIKE, LEFT OUT,
AND I DON'T AT ALL.

139
00:06:13,073 --> 00:06:15,508
THESE TWO GIRLS JUST MAKE ME
FEEL RIGHT AT HOME.

140
00:06:15,508 --> 00:06:18,411
Adrianne:
SHANNON, COME HERE, BABY.

141
00:06:18,411 --> 00:06:20,080
I WON'T LEAVE YOU OUT.

142
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,348
Shannon: THANKS.

143
00:06:21,348 --> 00:06:26,519
♪♪

144
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:32,425
Shannon: OH, MY GOSH,
WE HAVE MAIL, LADIES.

145
00:06:32,425 --> 00:06:36,296
Adrianne: HAND IT TO ME,
AND I WILL READ IT.

146
00:06:36,296 --> 00:06:38,598
Shannon: "YOU HAVE A FASHION
SHOW CASTING TONIGHT AT 8:00 PM.

147
00:06:38,598 --> 00:06:40,000
"HAVE YOUR HAIR AND MAKEUP DONE,

148
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,336
BE DRESSED AND IN THE HEELS
BY 7:30 PM."

149
00:06:44,137 --> 00:06:45,205
Tyra: GUYS, YOU'RE GONNA BE
DOING A GO SEE

150
00:06:45,205 --> 00:06:46,606
WITH BABY PHAT FASHIONS.

151
00:06:46,606 --> 00:06:47,707
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO TAKE YOUR
PERSONAL STYLE

152
00:06:47,707 --> 00:06:50,410
AND INCORPORATE WHAT KIMORA
CALLS THE STOMP,

153
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:53,313
WHEN YOU SHOW YOUR RUNWAY WALK
AT YOUR AUDITION.

154
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:54,714
SO I'M GONNA SHOW YOU WHAT IT
IS, ALL RIGHT?

155
00:06:54,714 --> 00:06:56,182
HERE'S A STOMP.

156
00:06:59,286 --> 00:07:02,589
GET TO THE END, AND YOU'RE LIKE,
POW! WHAT? SO? AND?

157
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:06,660
AND JUST FEEL MY STRIDE AND SEE,
MY HIP IS KIND OF DROPPING.

158
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,762
ELYSE COULD POTENTIALLY
ROCK THE FASHION WORLD.

159
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:12,365
SHE HAS SUCH A HIGH FASHION
EDITORIAL LOOK.

160
00:07:12,365 --> 00:07:15,368
I MEAN, SHE IS PERFECT FOR HIGH
FASHION,

161
00:07:15,368 --> 00:07:17,637
BUT I DON'T KNOW IF ELYSE REALLY
WANTS THIS ENOUGH.

162
00:07:17,637 --> 00:07:20,473
AND GIRLS THAT ARE AMBIVALENT
ARE USUALLY NOT SUCCESSFUL.

163
00:07:20,473 --> 00:07:22,142
Adrianne: SHE HATES MODELING.

164
00:07:22,142 --> 00:07:25,979
SHE HATES DOING EVERYTHING WE
DO, YET SHE'S THE BEST AT IT.

165
00:07:25,979 --> 00:07:28,315
Tyra: LONGER STRIDES.

166
00:07:28,315 --> 00:07:31,151
SHANNON IS ALL WARM AND FUZZY
AND ALL-AMERICAN.

167
00:07:31,151 --> 00:07:33,286
I MEAN, HER SMILE IS JUST LIKE,
BING!

168
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:34,688
IN ORDER FOR HER TO BE
SUCCESSFUL

169
00:07:34,688 --> 00:07:36,756
AND TAKE IT TO THE NEXT LEVEL,
SHE'S GONNA HAVE TO BECOME

170
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:39,225
MORE EDGY, MORE INTERESTING.

171
00:07:39,225 --> 00:07:41,594
AT TIMES I THOUGHT THAT SHANNON
WOULD WIN THE COMPETITION,

172
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:43,730
BUT SHANNON CHOSE NOT TO
PARTICIPATE

173
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:45,565
IN THE LAST PHOTO SHOOT,
AND NOW I THINK THAT

174
00:07:45,565 --> 00:07:48,969
SHE'S ESSENTIALLY ELIMINATED
HERSELF FROM THE COMPETITION.

175
00:07:48,969 --> 00:07:51,671
Tyra: ADRIANNE HAS COME SUCH A
LONG WAY,

176
00:07:51,671 --> 00:07:53,373
AND SHE REALLY WANTS THIS,

177
00:07:53,373 --> 00:07:56,343
BUT SHE'S STILL
SO ROUGH AROUND THE EDGES.

178
00:07:56,343 --> 00:07:59,045
SHE NEEDS A LOT OF POLISHING.

179
00:07:59,045 --> 00:08:00,313
Shannon: WHAT I LIKE ABOUT
ADRIANNE IS THAT

180
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:01,648
SHE DOESN'T CARE WHAT OTHERS
THINK OF HER.

181
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:04,317
SHE'S GONNA BE WHO SHE IS NO
MATTER WHAT.

182
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:06,419
Tyra: I HAVE
NO IDEA WHO'S GONNA WIN.

183
00:08:06,419 --> 00:08:09,990
ABSOLUTELY NO IDEA,
AND I LOVE THAT.

184
00:08:18,031 --> 00:08:23,970
♪♪

185
00:08:28,441 --> 00:08:30,010
Elyse: TODAY WE'RE GONNA HAVE A
GO-AND-SEE

186
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:34,014
FOR A CASTING CALL FOR A BABY
PHAT FASHION SHOW.

187
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:35,248
HOW ARE YOU GUYS?

188
00:08:35,248 --> 00:08:38,051
THANK YOU FOR COMING
TO THE HOUSE OF BABY PHAT.

189
00:08:38,051 --> 00:08:39,686
I'VE BEEN CASTING ALL DAY,
I'M DOING A FASHION SHOW.

190
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:41,755
YOU GUYS HAVE
TO GIVE IT ALL YOU GOT,

191
00:08:41,755 --> 00:08:44,691
JUST LIKE THE OTHER HUNDREDS OF
GIRLS WE'VE BEEN LOOKING AT.

192
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:47,293
SO I GUESS WE'RE GONNA TAKE
EVERYTHING THAT WE HAVE DONE

193
00:08:47,293 --> 00:08:50,030
THUS FAR AND SEE
WHAT YOU GUYS GOT.

194
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,664
ADRIANNE, PLEASE COME IN.

195
00:08:51,664 --> 00:08:53,600
OKAY, SO WE'LL START FROM HERE,
AND TURN AROUND

196
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,969
AND WALK DOWN THAT WAY AND THEN
WALK BACK TOWARDS US.

197
00:08:55,969 --> 00:08:59,472
♪♪

198
00:08:59,472 --> 00:09:02,108
JUST TURN, COME BACK.

199
00:09:02,108 --> 00:09:04,411
BABY PHAT, I DIDN'T THINK
I DID A GOOD JOB.

200
00:09:04,411 --> 00:09:07,313
I'M ALWAYS TOLD
THAT I WALK LIKE A MAN.

201
00:09:07,313 --> 00:09:09,315
IT TAKES YOU ABOUT FIVE MINUTES
OF WARMING UP,

202
00:09:09,315 --> 00:09:10,150
AND THEN YOU COME TOGETHER.

203
00:09:10,150 --> 00:09:11,518
YEAH.
YEAH.

204
00:09:11,518 --> 00:09:13,720
Kimora: OKAY, SHANNON.

205
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:16,056
Shannon: I WAS MORE EXCITED THAN
NERVOUS, ACTUALLY,

206
00:09:16,056 --> 00:09:18,091
PROBABLY 'CAUSE PRACTICE-- YOU
KNOW, WHEN YOU PRACTICE

207
00:09:18,091 --> 00:09:21,661
A LITTLE BIT MORE, YOU GET MORE
CONFIDENT IN YOURSELF.

208
00:09:21,661 --> 00:09:23,530
COME TOGETHER, GIRL,
I AIN'T MAD AT YA.

209
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:24,597
YEAH.

210
00:09:24,597 --> 00:09:25,732
YOU PULLIN' IT TOGETHER.

211
00:09:25,732 --> 00:09:27,434
OH, YOU PULLING IT TOGETHER,
OKAY.

212
00:09:27,434 --> 00:09:28,968
THAT'S VERY NICE, SHANNON,
YOU'VE BEEN PRACTICING.

213
00:09:28,968 --> 00:09:30,236
PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT.

214
00:09:31,371 --> 00:09:34,007
Kimora: HI, ELYSE.
Elyse: HI.

215
00:09:34,007 --> 00:09:35,275
Kimora: YOU START HERE AND GO
ALL THE WAY TO THE END

216
00:09:35,275 --> 00:09:39,579
AND COME ALL THE WAY BACK LIKE
YOU DID.

217
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,181
YOU GUYS ARE WALKING BETTER THAN
ME, HONEY,

218
00:09:41,181 --> 00:09:43,049
AND IT'S BEEN A LONG TIME.

219
00:09:43,049 --> 00:09:44,084
ARE YOU NERVOUS?
DON'T BE NERVOUS.

220
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:45,251
I'M A LITTLE NERVOUS.

221
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,319
OH, MY GOD, HOW LONG HAVE WE
BEEN TOGETHER?

222
00:09:46,319 --> 00:09:47,287
YOU'RE NERVOUS, GIRL.

223
00:09:47,287 --> 00:09:48,688
RELAX YOUR FINGERS.

224
00:09:48,688 --> 00:09:50,356
'CAUSE YOU WALK LIKE YOU HAVE
DIRTY NAPKINS OR TISSUES.

225
00:09:50,356 --> 00:09:51,391
THAT'S ME, I ALWAYS HAVE...

226
00:09:51,391 --> 00:09:53,293
IT'S NOT SEXY.

227
00:09:53,293 --> 00:09:54,527
Kimora: YOU ALL DID VERY WELL.

228
00:09:54,527 --> 00:09:56,596
I WAS VERY, VERY IMPRESSED.

229
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:58,431
BYE, YOU GUYS,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

230
00:09:58,431 --> 00:09:59,632
YOU GUYS WERE WONDERFUL.
Shannon: THANKS.

231
00:09:59,632 --> 00:10:06,306
♪♪

232
00:10:06,306 --> 00:10:08,308
WE HAVE MAIL!
I LOVE GETTING MAIL.

233
00:10:08,308 --> 00:10:09,742
Adrianne: WHO WANTS TO READ IT?

234
00:10:09,742 --> 00:10:11,544
ELYSE?

235
00:10:11,544 --> 00:10:14,114
"TWO OF YOU WILL CONTINUE ON TO
BECOME AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

236
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:15,982
ONE OF YOU
WILL BE ELIMINATED."

237
00:10:15,982 --> 00:10:17,050
Adrianne: ISN'T THAT WEIRD?

238
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:20,386
REMEMBER WHEN IT SAID
"NINE OF YOU"?

239
00:10:20,587 --> 00:10:21,521
Shannon: YEAH.

240
00:10:21,521 --> 00:10:22,722
Adrianne: NOW IT SAYS TWO.

241
00:10:22,722 --> 00:10:24,124
I THINK I DESERVE IT BECAUSE

242
00:10:24,124 --> 00:10:27,327
I CAME A REALLY LONG WAY SINCE I
CAME HERE.

243
00:10:27,327 --> 00:10:31,764
I'VE JUST TRIED TO DO MY BEST
EVERY TIME WE DO ANYTHING.

244
00:10:31,764 --> 00:10:33,766
Shannon: WHEN YOU GIVE SOMETHING
LIKE YOUR BEST,

245
00:10:33,766 --> 00:10:35,335
YOU JUST GIVE YOUR ALL AND YOU
FEEL LIKE

246
00:10:35,335 --> 00:10:37,036
YOU SHOULD BE REWARDED FOR THAT.

247
00:10:37,036 --> 00:10:40,173
Elyse: I DON'T THINK THAT IT'S
ACCEPTABLE TO SAY

248
00:10:40,173 --> 00:10:42,542
THAT ANYONE DESERVES TO WIN
THIS COMPETITION.

249
00:10:42,542 --> 00:10:46,346
IT'S REALLY NOT A BASIC HUMAN
RIGHT TO, UM,

250
00:10:46,346 --> 00:10:48,348
GET A MODELING CONTRACT.

251
00:10:48,348 --> 00:10:53,653
♪♪

252
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:55,588
Tyra: HELLO, EVERYBODY.

253
00:10:55,588 --> 00:10:58,992
TONIGHT IS A SPECIAL ELIMINATION
BECAUSE TONIGHT

254
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,127
THERE WILL ONLY BE TWO GIRLS
LEFT STANDING,

255
00:11:01,127 --> 00:11:05,431
AND THOSE TWO GIRLS WILL COMPETE
IN A BABY PHAT FASHION SHOW.

256
00:11:05,431 --> 00:11:08,001
YOUR PERFORMANCE IN THAT FASHION
SHOW WILL HELP DETERMINE

257
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:10,503
WHO WILL BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

258
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:13,339
NOW AS USUAL, WE HAVE OUR PANEL
OF CRAZY-ASS JUDGES.

259
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:15,141
FIRST, WE HAVE JANICE DICKINSON.

260
00:11:15,141 --> 00:11:17,343
JANICE IS THE ONE OF THE WORLD'S
FIRST SUPERMODELS.

261
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:18,745
WE HAVE BEAU QUILLIAN.

262
00:11:18,745 --> 00:11:21,414
BEAU IS A FASHION EDITOR AT
"MARIE CLAIRE."

263
00:11:21,414 --> 00:11:23,016
WE HAVE KIMORA LEE SIMMONS.

264
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:26,519
KIMORA IS THE CREATIVE DIRECTOR
AND OWNER OF BABY PHAT FASHIONS.

265
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:29,422
AND LAST BUT NOT LEAST, WE HAVE
A SPECIAL JUDGE-- DREW LINEHAN.

266
00:11:29,422 --> 00:11:33,293
DREW'S A FASHION SHOW CASTING
DIRECTOR AND A PRODUCER.

267
00:11:33,293 --> 00:11:36,262
WE'LL BRING YOU IN ONE BY ONE
FOR INDIVIDUAL EVALUATIONS,

268
00:11:36,262 --> 00:11:37,597
AND, ELYSE, YOU'RE FIRST.

269
00:11:37,597 --> 00:11:39,699
OKAY.

270
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:41,034
JUST SHOW US, YOU KNOW,

271
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:43,036
WHAT YOU THINK YOU'VE LEARNED IN
TERMS OF POSING.

272
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:47,674
♪♪

273
00:11:47,674 --> 00:11:49,075
Tyra: THANK YOU.

274
00:11:49,075 --> 00:11:51,678
Drew: SO, ELYSE,
WHAT DROVE YOU TO THIS?

275
00:11:51,678 --> 00:11:54,480
I TRIED OUT FOR THIS ON
JUST A TOTAL WHIM.

276
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,216
THEY HAD THE AUDITION AT THIS
SILLY LITTLE PLACE.

277
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:57,650
IT WAS RIGHT BY MY HOUSE, AND,
LIKE, YOU KNOW,

278
00:11:57,650 --> 00:12:00,320
I JUST-- I THOUGHT
IT WOULD BE FUN.

279
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,721
WHAT REALLY HAVE YOU LEARNED?

280
00:12:01,721 --> 00:12:03,256
WHERE DO YOU THINK YOU'VE
PROGRESSED

281
00:12:03,256 --> 00:12:04,657
FROM WHERE YOU STARTED?

282
00:12:04,657 --> 00:12:06,025
Elyse: THE FIRST THING I LEARNED

283
00:12:06,025 --> 00:12:08,328
WAS JUST TO BE CONFIDENT AND TO
STOP THINKING

284
00:12:08,328 --> 00:12:10,763
OF MYSELF AS A NERD, TO BE A
MODEL INSIDE.

285
00:12:10,763 --> 00:12:14,267
IT WAS REALLY HARD FOR ME TO
ACCEPT CRITICISM,

286
00:12:14,267 --> 00:12:16,603
LIKE, ON A PHYSICAL BASIS, YOU
KNOW, BECAUSE I COME FROM THIS,

287
00:12:16,603 --> 00:12:19,239
LIKE, TOTALLY INTELLECTUAL,
MENTAL WORLD.

288
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:20,440
Tyra: EARLY ON, YOU WERE LIKE,

289
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:23,076
BEING A TOP MODEL IS JUST
STRICTLY PHYSICAL.

290
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:26,179
YOU SAID THAT MYSELF, CINDY
CRAWFORD, HEIDI KLUM,

291
00:12:26,179 --> 00:12:28,982
OTHER TOP MODELS-- THAT THE ONLY
REASON WHY WE WERE TOP MODELS

292
00:12:28,982 --> 00:12:31,117
IS THAT WE WERE THE BEST
PHYSICALLY LOOKING MODELS

293
00:12:31,117 --> 00:12:32,652
IN THE WORLD,
AND I DISAGREED WITH YOU.

294
00:12:32,652 --> 00:12:34,287
I DON'T KNOW, I DON'T THINK
THERE'S REALLY

295
00:12:34,287 --> 00:12:37,724
A LOT OF MERITS THAT ONE CAN
HAVE OUTSIDE OF THE PHYSICAL,

296
00:12:37,724 --> 00:12:39,058
AND I THINK I HAVE THOSE.

297
00:12:39,058 --> 00:12:40,326
Tyra: YOU DON'T
THINK THERE'S ANYTHING

298
00:12:40,326 --> 00:12:42,195
OUTSIDE OF THE PHYSICAL THAT
MAKES A SUPERMODEL?

299
00:12:42,195 --> 00:12:43,997
I DON'T THINK SO, NO.

300
00:12:43,997 --> 00:12:45,398
HOW DO YOU FEEL NOW?

301
00:12:45,398 --> 00:12:49,135
I DEFINITELY, UM, I STILL
BELIEVE IN ESTROGEN FEATURES,

302
00:12:49,135 --> 00:12:50,169
AND, YOU KNOW, ALL THAT STUFF.

303
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:50,970
WHY DON'T YOU BREAK THAT DOWN
FOR US?

304
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:52,438
Janice: WHAT'S THAT?

305
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:54,340
Elyse: IF YOU'VE HAD A LOT OF
ESTROGEN IN YOUR DEVELOPMENT,

306
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:57,010
IT CREATES A CERTAIN SORT OF
FACIAL FEATURES,

307
00:12:57,010 --> 00:13:00,079
AND THAT'S A SMALL JAW,
WIDER-SET EYES, BIGGER LIPS,

308
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:02,649
SMALLER EARS,
A SMALLER BROW RIDGE.

309
00:13:02,649 --> 00:13:06,252
SO IF YOU GAVE A MALE MODEL
ESTROGEN...

310
00:13:06,252 --> 00:13:08,588
Elyse: NO, YOU'D HAVE TO DO IT
WHEN HE WAS, LIKE, AN INFANT.

311
00:13:08,588 --> 00:13:10,223
Janice: WAY OVER MY HEAD,
SORRY, YOU GUYS.

312
00:13:10,223 --> 00:13:12,191
Kimora: ARE YOU PROPOSING THAT I
SHOULD GIVE MY BABY HORMONES?

313
00:13:12,191 --> 00:13:13,493
Elyse: DON'T DO IT.

314
00:13:13,493 --> 00:13:15,261
NO, I DON'T THINK YOU SHOULD DO
IT, BUT IT WOULD WORK.

315
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:19,699
Tyra: SO YOU THINK BEAUTY IS,
UM, SCIENTIFIC, HORMONAL?

316
00:13:19,699 --> 00:13:22,368
Elyse: I THINK A LOT
OF PHYSICAL BEAUTY IS.

317
00:13:22,368 --> 00:13:24,737
SEND ADRIANNE IN, PLEASE.

318
00:13:24,737 --> 00:13:26,506
Beau: IT'S OPERATION
ADRIANNE STORM.

319
00:13:26,506 --> 00:13:28,107
Janice: I DIG IT.

320
00:13:28,107 --> 00:13:30,410
Tyra: ALL RIGHT, ADRIANNE, THINK
ABOUT THESE LAST EIGHT WEEKS

321
00:13:30,410 --> 00:13:34,681
AND WHAT YOU'VE LEARNED
IN TERMS OF A PHOTO SHOOT.

322
00:13:34,681 --> 00:13:39,986
♪♪

323
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:41,220
Tyra: OKAY.

324
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,655
WHY DO YOU WANNA BE A MODEL?

325
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:45,158
I LOVE BEING THE CENTER OF
ATTENTION.

326
00:13:45,158 --> 00:13:47,593
IT MAKES ME-- OH, I CAN'T SAY
THAT.

327
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:49,329
Tyra: WHAT?

328
00:13:49,329 --> 00:13:51,230
Adrianne: IT MAKES ME FEEL LIKE
GOD.

329
00:13:51,230 --> 00:13:53,633
IT SORT OF IS, ISN'T IT?

330
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:55,301
YOU THINK YOU'RE READY TO DO
A REAL FASHION SHOW?

331
00:13:55,301 --> 00:13:57,470
LIKE A BIG FASHION SHOW WITH THE
BIGGEST MODELS IN THE WORLD

332
00:13:57,470 --> 00:13:59,405
IN FRONT OF THOUSANDS OF PEOPLE?

333
00:13:59,405 --> 00:14:03,543
WITH CUTTHROAT MODELS TRYING TO
KNOCK YOU OFF THE RUNWAY?

334
00:14:03,543 --> 00:14:05,144
WITH ALL OF THE MOST IMPORTANT
EDITORS

335
00:14:05,144 --> 00:14:06,979
AND PHOTOGRAPHERS, BUYERS?
Janice: IN THE FRONT ROW?

336
00:14:06,979 --> 00:14:08,548
Adrianne: I WOULDN'T BE NERVOUS
AT ALL WITH PEOPLE.

337
00:14:08,548 --> 00:14:10,083
I'M REALLY NOT, I MEAN--

338
00:14:10,083 --> 00:14:11,351
Tyra: IN 4-INCH STILETTOS?

339
00:14:11,351 --> 00:14:13,686
Adrianne: NO, NOT REALLY.

340
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:15,221
I CAN RUN IN 4-INCH STILETTOS.

341
00:14:15,221 --> 00:14:16,556
Janice: COOL.

342
00:14:16,556 --> 00:14:17,557
Beau: I WOULD JUST SAY ONE
LITTLE THING.

343
00:14:17,557 --> 00:14:20,326
WHEN YOU DO THE, UM, YOU HAVE--

344
00:14:20,326 --> 00:14:22,428
YOU DO YOUR, LIKE, GOOFY SMILE
LIKE...

345
00:14:22,428 --> 00:14:23,996
DON'T DO THAT.

346
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:25,164
Adrianne: I DON'T KNOW WHAT
YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

347
00:14:25,164 --> 00:14:26,199
Tyra: OH, THIS ONE.

348
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:28,067
Janice:: I LIKE THE GOOFY SMILE.

349
00:14:28,067 --> 00:14:29,702
I THINK IT'S CUTE.

350
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:31,971
Adrianne: BYE, GUYS.

351
00:14:31,971 --> 00:14:34,040
Tyra: MISS SHANNON COMING IN
HERE, LOOKING LIKE A REAL MODEL.

352
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,108
Shannon: I'M TRYIN'.

353
00:14:35,108 --> 00:14:36,509
Janice: GUESS WHAT, TYRA.

354
00:14:36,509 --> 00:14:38,444
HER HAIR IS SLICKED BACK, HELLO!

355
00:14:38,444 --> 00:14:40,246
Tyra: FIRST THING I SAW.

356
00:14:40,246 --> 00:14:41,481
LOOKS REALLY PRETTY BACK.

357
00:14:41,481 --> 00:14:42,281
Shannon: THANK YOU.

358
00:14:42,281 --> 00:14:44,083
MAKES YOUR NECK VERY LONG.

359
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:45,485
Tyra: I WANT YOU TO WORK ABOUT
THREE POSES OF YOUR FACE.

360
00:14:45,485 --> 00:14:51,691
♪♪

361
00:14:51,691 --> 00:14:54,360
TOOTHPASTE COMPANIES OUT THERE,
THIS IS YOUR GIRL.

362
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,129
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY.

363
00:14:56,129 --> 00:14:58,231
CAN YOU NAME THREE PHOTOGRAPHERS
WHO SHOOT FASHION SPREADS

364
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:00,299
FOR "VOGUE" MAGAZINE?

365
00:15:00,299 --> 00:15:01,567
Shannon: I'M SORRY, I CAN'T.

366
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:04,303
WHAT ABOUT SOMEBODY YOU'VE
WORKED WITH?

367
00:15:04,303 --> 00:15:06,072
(squealing)
OH, MY GOSH.

368
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:09,575
YOU HAVE TO KNOW THE INDUSTRY IF
YOU WANNA BE A TOP MODEL.

369
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:11,244
Drew: DO YOU KNOW YOUR
MEASUREMENTS?

370
00:15:11,244 --> 00:15:12,612
NO, I DON'T.

371
00:15:12,612 --> 00:15:14,013
Tyra: YOU SHOULD KNOW YOUR REAL
MEASUREMENTS.

372
00:15:14,013 --> 00:15:14,747
AND YOU SHOULD KNOW YOUR FAKE
MEASUREMENTS.

373
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,549
Kimora: WHAT YOU SAY!

374
00:15:16,549 --> 00:15:17,717
Tyra: YOU KNOW, THERE'S THE FAKE
ONES TO GIVE TO THE CLIENTS

375
00:15:17,717 --> 00:15:19,185
AND THEN THERE'S THE REAL ONES
WHEN YOU'RE DOING,

376
00:15:19,185 --> 00:15:20,386
LIKE, THE MEASUREMENT.

377
00:15:20,386 --> 00:15:21,387
OKAY, SHANNON.
Kimora: THANK YOU.

378
00:15:21,387 --> 00:15:22,422
THANKS, SHANNON.
Shannon: THANK YOU.

379
00:15:24,724 --> 00:15:26,459
Tyra: START WITH ELYSE.

380
00:15:26,459 --> 00:15:30,062
Kimora: ELYSE CAME OFF LIKE A
BIG KNOW-IT-ALL TODAY.

381
00:15:30,062 --> 00:15:32,565
IT COULD WORK FOR HER OR IT
COULD WORK AGAINST HER.

382
00:15:32,565 --> 00:15:33,599
ONCE SHE GETS OUT THERE IN THE
FIELD,

383
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:35,067
SHE'LL FIND OUT REAL FAST.

384
00:15:35,067 --> 00:15:36,335
Tyra: I LOVE ELYSE'S
INTELLIGENCE,

385
00:15:36,335 --> 00:15:38,137
BUT SHE COMES OFF REALLY EDGY.

386
00:15:38,137 --> 00:15:41,174
SOMETIMES TO BE A TOP MODEL, YOU
NEED TO BE EDGY AND COMMERCIAL.

387
00:15:41,174 --> 00:15:43,709
Drew: I'M NOT SURE ABOUT
SUPERIORITY, BUT SHE REALLY IS,

388
00:15:43,709 --> 00:15:46,446
OBVIOUSLY, THE MOST HIGH FASHION
OUT OF THE GROUP.

389
00:15:46,446 --> 00:15:49,115
Tyra: I'M JUST TORN BECAUSE THE
TITLE OF THE SHOW

390
00:15:49,115 --> 00:15:51,350
AND WHAT THE MEANING OF THE SHOW
IS "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

391
00:15:51,350 --> 00:15:53,152
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL" IS
NOT JUST BEING

392
00:15:53,152 --> 00:15:54,587
A HIGH-FASHION MODEL.

393
00:15:54,587 --> 00:15:56,322
SHE'S MORE
OF A COMMERCIAL MODEL.

394
00:15:56,322 --> 00:15:57,457
SHE DOES "SPORTS ILLUSTRATED,"

395
00:15:57,457 --> 00:15:59,625
SHE DOES VICTORIA SECRET,
REVLON ADS.

396
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:01,527
DREW, I'M NOT SURE
SHE HAS THE COMMITMENT.

397
00:16:01,527 --> 00:16:04,297
MEAN, COME ON, SHE FEEL ASLEEP
WHILE YOU WERE TALKING TO HER.

398
00:16:04,297 --> 00:16:06,466
Beau: OUT.
Janice: IN!

399
00:16:08,334 --> 00:16:09,969
Tyra: THIS IS-- ADRIANNE IS
INTERESTING TO ME

400
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:12,405
BECAUSE WHEN SHE FIRST WALKED
INTO THE SEMI-FINALS

401
00:16:12,405 --> 00:16:15,441
IN LOS ANGELES, LIKE, SHE WAS
NOT A LOOKER.

402
00:16:15,441 --> 00:16:17,076
Janice: SHE DIDN'T WALK,
SHE HOOFED.

403
00:16:17,076 --> 00:16:18,277
Tyra: I MEAN, LOOK AT THAT.

404
00:16:18,277 --> 00:16:19,412
I REALLY ADMIRE HER
TRANSFORMATION.

405
00:16:19,412 --> 00:16:20,980
Beau: THE CAMERA LOVES HER,

406
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:23,082
SO I WOULDN'T EVER HAVE ANY
PROBLEMS WORKING WITH HER.

407
00:16:23,082 --> 00:16:24,317
I'M NOT SO SURE.

408
00:16:24,317 --> 00:16:26,519
SHE DOESN'T REALLY SELL ME.

409
00:16:26,519 --> 00:16:27,987
ADRIANNE'S IN.

410
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,055
OUT.

411
00:16:30,256 --> 00:16:32,458
Janice: (sighing) I'M DYIN'.

412
00:16:32,758 --> 00:16:34,627
Tyra: I THINK SHANNON'S THE ONLY
ONE THAT I CAN SEE

413
00:16:34,627 --> 00:16:38,598
BEING ON THE COUCH OF JAY LENO
OR DAVID LETTERMAN OR--

414
00:16:38,598 --> 00:16:40,500
NO, NOT KNOWING THE
PHOTOGRAPHERS

415
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:43,302
IS SORT OF NOT ACCEPTABLE.

416
00:16:43,302 --> 00:16:46,305
Beau: YOU KNOW, I DO THINK THAT
THE CAMERA...

417
00:16:46,305 --> 00:16:48,040
LOVES HER FACE.
LOVES HER FACE.

418
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:49,208
Tyra: YOU CAN TAKE A COMMERCIAL
GIRL

419
00:16:49,208 --> 00:16:51,577
AND MAKE HER MORE HIGH FASHION.

420
00:16:51,577 --> 00:16:54,146
I JUST DON'T KNOW IF IT'S
POSSIBLE TO DO THAT

421
00:16:54,146 --> 00:16:57,250
IN A COUPLE OF DAYS, 'CAUSE
THAT'S ALL WE HAVE LEFT.

422
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:59,118
I HATE THESE CUTS!

423
00:16:59,118 --> 00:17:00,353
THEY DRIVE ME CRAZY!

424
00:17:03,256 --> 00:17:07,460
Tyra: IT WILL BE INCREDIBLY HARD
TO SAY GOODBYE

425
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,761
TO ONE OF YOU TONIGHT.

426
00:17:08,761 --> 00:17:11,696
WE'VE ALL BEEN TOGETHER
A VERY LONG TIME.

427
00:17:11,696 --> 00:17:13,366
WE'VE BEEN AROUND THE WORLD
AND BACK AGAIN.

428
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:15,667
THERE ARE THREE OF YOU LEFT.

429
00:17:15,667 --> 00:17:18,204
THREE BEAUTIFUL YOUNG LADIES
STANDING IN FRONT OF ME,

430
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:19,672
BUT ONLY TWO OF YOU ARE STILL IN
THE RUNNING

431
00:17:19,672 --> 00:17:22,141
TO BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

432
00:17:22,141 --> 00:17:23,242
HOW BAD DO YOU WANT THIS?

433
00:17:23,242 --> 00:17:26,045
HOW BAD DO YOU WANT THIS,
ADRIANNE?

434
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:29,215
REAL DAMN BAD, TYRA BANKS.

435
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:35,087
IT'S JUST BEEN A LONG, STRANGE
TRIP, AND IF I WIN, HELL, YEAH.

436
00:17:35,087 --> 00:17:36,622
SHANNON?

437
00:17:36,622 --> 00:17:39,225
WORDS CANNOT EXPRESS
HOW BAD I WANT THIS.

438
00:17:39,225 --> 00:17:41,060
I'M NERVOUS AND EXCITED.

439
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,162
I'M HAVING THE MINDSET THAT I
REALLY, REALLY, REALLY, REALLY,

440
00:17:43,162 --> 00:17:45,031
REALLY WANNA STAY HERE, BUT
THEN, LIKE,

441
00:17:45,031 --> 00:17:46,532
WHEN THEY'RE CALLING EACH
OTHER'S NAMES,

442
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:48,234
YOU HAVE TO GET YOURSELF
PREPARED, BECAUSE YOU DON'T

443
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:51,237
WANNA BE HEARTBROKEN IF YOU ARE
ONE OF THE GIRLS TO LEAVE.

444
00:17:51,237 --> 00:17:52,538
ELYSE?

445
00:17:52,538 --> 00:17:55,441
DAMN BAD, MISS TYRA.

446
00:17:55,441 --> 00:17:57,076
Elyse: AT THIS POINT, I DON'T
HAVE ANY PREDICTIONS

447
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,345
AS TO WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED,
BUT SHANNON DID TELL ME

448
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:02,481
THAT JESUS TOLD HER THAT I WOULD
BE STAYING HERE SO

449
00:18:02,481 --> 00:18:05,084
THAT MAKES ME FEEL PRETTY
COMFORTABLE.

450
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:07,019
TONIGHT'S ELIMINATION WILL
DETERMINE WHICH TWO GIRLS

451
00:18:07,019 --> 00:18:11,157
WILL VIE FOR THE TITLE OF
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL

452
00:18:11,157 --> 00:18:17,496
AT A FINAL HUGE FASHION SHOW
HERE IN NEW YORK CITY.

453
00:18:17,496 --> 00:18:18,531
SHANNON.

454
00:18:24,236 --> 00:18:26,439
Tyra: SHANNON,
IF YOU WANT THIS BAD,

455
00:18:26,439 --> 00:18:29,709
YOU HAVE TO STUDY BAD.

456
00:18:29,709 --> 00:18:34,513
YOU HAVE TO LIVE AND BREATHE
THIS INDUSTRY.

457
00:18:34,513 --> 00:18:37,350
CONGRATULATIONS.

458
00:18:37,350 --> 00:18:38,584
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING

459
00:18:38,584 --> 00:18:39,518
TOWARDS BECOMING AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

460
00:18:39,518 --> 00:18:40,519
THANK YOU.

461
00:18:46,993 --> 00:18:49,495
WILL ELYSE AND ADRIANNE PLEASE
STEP FORWARD?

462
00:18:51,564 --> 00:18:52,999
Adrianne: THAT REALLY SUCKED.

463
00:18:52,999 --> 00:18:55,568
I DIDN'T LIKE GOING UP AGAINST
ELYSE.

464
00:18:55,568 --> 00:18:57,436
I ALWAYS TOLD MYSELF
IF ELYSE AND I

465
00:18:57,436 --> 00:18:59,005
EVER WENT UP AGAINST EACH OTHER,

466
00:18:59,005 --> 00:19:02,508
THAT SHE WOULD BE THE ONE WHO
WOULD GET CHOSEN.

467
00:19:02,508 --> 00:19:07,013
Elyse: ADRIANNE'S DEFINITELY MY
CLOSEST ALLY IN THE HOUSE,

468
00:19:07,013 --> 00:19:09,382
BUT I THINK THAT ADRIANNE IS
REALLY EXPECTING TO WIN.

469
00:19:09,382 --> 00:19:11,350
ADRIANNE, I KNOW THE PANEL HAS
REALLY STAYED

470
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:13,319
ON TOP OF YOU ABOUT YOUR SPEECH.

471
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:18,057
SPEECH IS SO IMPORTANT, SO WORK
ON THAT EVEN MORE.

472
00:19:18,057 --> 00:19:20,493
ELYSE...

473
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:23,996
ELYSE, YOUR LOOK IS REALLY
STRONG FOR THE FASHION WORLD,

474
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:27,333
FOR THE HARD-CORE, DIE-HARD
FASHION WORLD.

475
00:19:27,333 --> 00:19:29,168
BUT IN ORDER TO BE A MORE
COMMERCIAL MODEL,

476
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:32,271
A MODEL THAT APPEALS TO THE
MASSES OF AMERICA,

477
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:34,473
YOU'VE GOTTA SOFTEN UP YOUR LOOK
A LITTLE BIT.

478
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:36,542
ELYSE, I ADMIRE YOUR
INTELLIGENCE.

479
00:19:36,542 --> 00:19:39,979
I THINK YOU ARE SO SMART.

480
00:19:39,979 --> 00:19:41,213
BUT ONE THING WITH THAT
INTELLIGENCE IS

481
00:19:41,213 --> 00:19:43,449
IT CAN INTIMIDATE PEOPLE,

482
00:19:43,449 --> 00:19:48,120
AND THERE'S A WAY TO USE THAT
INTELLIGENCE IN A WAY

483
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:50,156
THAT DOESN'T FEEL LIKE YOU'RE
MAYBE PUTTING DOWN OTHER PEOPLE

484
00:19:50,156 --> 00:19:53,359
OR SOUNDING DEROGATORY.

485
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:01,100
ADRIANNE, CONGRATULATIONS.

486
00:20:09,642 --> 00:20:10,976
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING
TOWARDS BECOMING

487
00:20:10,976 --> 00:20:12,611
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

488
00:20:12,611 --> 00:20:14,447
Adrianne: THANK YOU.

489
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,285
Elyse: TYRA TOLD ME THAT I WAS
ARROGANT AND CONDESCENDING

490
00:20:19,285 --> 00:20:21,987
IN MY SPEECH AND IN MY
INTERACTIONS WITH OTHERS

491
00:20:21,987 --> 00:20:23,389
AND I THINK...

492
00:20:23,389 --> 00:20:25,725
SHE WAS RIGHT.

493
00:20:25,725 --> 00:20:28,194
I CAN'T SAY THAT IT FEELS GOOD
TO BE ELIMINATED,

494
00:20:28,194 --> 00:20:29,729
BUT I ALSO CAN'T DENY THAT
THERE'S A CERTAIN

495
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:33,766
SENSE OF RELIEF THAT COMES
WITH IT.

496
00:20:33,766 --> 00:20:36,068
YOU KNOW,
IT SUCKS TO LOSE AT ANYTHING,

497
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:38,571
BUT THE DECISION
HAS BEEN MADE FOR ME,

498
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:41,407
AND I'LL BE A DOCTOR
AND NOT A TOP MODEL.

499
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:43,175
Tyra: THIS IS THE REAL DEAL NOW.

500
00:20:43,175 --> 00:20:44,677
Janice: THIS IS IT.

501
00:20:44,677 --> 00:20:47,213
Tyra: THIS IS NO JOKE,
THIS IS REAL.

502
00:20:47,213 --> 00:20:50,015
Janice: NO KIDDING.

503
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:53,052
Elyse: COMING INTO THIS WORLD OF
MODELING WAS THE RESULT

504
00:20:53,052 --> 00:20:56,722
OF A BIZARRE CHAIN OF EVENTS
THAT I CAN ONLY DESCRIBE

505
00:20:56,722 --> 00:20:58,591
AS FLUKEY IN EVERY
SENSE OF THE WORD,

506
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:02,128
SO WHEN I LEAVE,
I'LL BE GONE FOREVER.

507
00:21:11,203 --> 00:21:23,482
♪♪

508
00:21:23,482 --> 00:21:25,184
Shannon: HI.

509
00:21:25,184 --> 00:21:26,519
WE NEED SOME HELP
ON OUR HAIR, I GUESS.

510
00:21:32,057 --> 00:21:34,059
Shannon: WE'RE GONNA BE IN A
FASHION SHOW TOMORROW.

511
00:21:34,059 --> 00:21:35,594
WE'RE A LITTLE BIT NERVOUS.

512
00:21:35,594 --> 00:21:38,197
I COULDN'T SLEEP LAST NIGHT.

513
00:21:38,197 --> 00:21:44,236
IT WAS A WEIRD MIXTURE OF
OVERJOYNESS AND BEING UPSET.

514
00:21:44,236 --> 00:21:46,505
I WOULD THINK I WOULD GO HOME UP
AGAINST ELYSE, JUST BECAUSE

515
00:21:46,505 --> 00:21:50,743
SHE'S A GENIUS,
AND I'M A HIGH SCHOOL DROPOUT.

516
00:21:53,012 --> 00:21:54,280
Antekqua:
WHAT DO YOU GUYS THINK?

517
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:56,115
WE ARE READY.

518
00:21:56,115 --> 00:21:57,650
BYE, THANK YOU SO MUCH.
Adrianne: LATER, ANTEKQUA.

519
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:02,588
Shannon: "TONIGHT WE WILL BE
HAVING DINNER AT BLUE FIN.

520
00:22:02,588 --> 00:22:05,057
PLEASE BE READY AT 7:00 P.M.

521
00:22:05,057 --> 00:22:07,026
TYRA!

522
00:22:07,026 --> 00:22:09,695
NOT EVEN 20 MINUTES TO GET
READY.

523
00:22:09,695 --> 00:22:11,096
CAN I USE THIS FOR TWO SECONDS?

524
00:22:11,096 --> 00:22:12,164
NO.

525
00:22:14,433 --> 00:22:16,302
COME ON, HAIR, WORK WITH ME.

526
00:22:18,270 --> 00:22:19,605
Tyra: HEY!

527
00:22:19,605 --> 00:22:21,407
Adrianne: HEY.
Shannon: HI!

528
00:22:21,407 --> 00:22:22,675
Tyra: I THOUGHT THE GIRLS WOULD
BE REALLY NERVOUS

529
00:22:22,675 --> 00:22:25,044
THE NIGHT BEFORE THE BABY PHAT
FASHION SHOW,

530
00:22:25,044 --> 00:22:26,579
SO I INVITED THEM TO A SWANKY
DINNER

531
00:22:26,579 --> 00:22:31,050
WITH MAKEUP MAESTRO JAY MANUEL
AND RUNWAY DIVA J. ALEXANDER

532
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:33,285
Jay: YOU KNOW, REALLY, IT'S GOOD
TO BE SURPRISED.

533
00:22:33,285 --> 00:22:34,520
SERIOUSLY, SHANNON.

534
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:36,655
SHE'S NEVER HAD SUSHI BEFORE.

535
00:22:38,290 --> 00:22:40,259
Adrianne: I JUST ATE, LIKE--
Shannon: YOU LIKE IT?

536
00:22:40,259 --> 00:22:41,760
OH, SHOOT.

537
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:44,330
Tyra: WHEN YOU FIRST CAME IN AND
YOU SAW THE TEN GIRLS,

538
00:22:44,330 --> 00:22:47,166
WHO DID YOU THINK WOULD HAVE
BEEN YOUR MOST COMPETITION?

539
00:22:47,166 --> 00:22:50,369
Shannon: WHEN I SAW TESSA LEAVE,
I WAS JUST LIKE, OH, MY WORD.

540
00:22:50,369 --> 00:22:52,972
Tyra: SO WHAT WAS THE TOUGHEST
PART OF BEING IN THE PENTHOUSE?

541
00:22:52,972 --> 00:22:55,641
Adrianne: LIVING WITH KATIE
THE ENTIRE TIME.

542
00:22:55,641 --> 00:22:57,076
Tyra: WHY DO YOU HATE KATIE?

543
00:22:57,076 --> 00:22:58,978
Adrianne: KATIE DID
NOT LIKE ME, MAN.

544
00:22:58,978 --> 00:23:00,346
Tyra: WHY NOT?

545
00:23:00,346 --> 00:23:02,281
Adrianne: I FELT LIKE SHE
THOUGHT I WAS REALLY GHETTO.

546
00:23:02,281 --> 00:23:04,483
WELL...

547
00:23:04,483 --> 00:23:05,551
Jay: WELL, WE KNOW WHO REALLY
EXPECTED

548
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:07,720
TO BE ONE OF THE LAST TWO--
NICOLE.

549
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:08,721
Tyra: OH, NICOLE.

550
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:10,022
Jay: SHE WAS REALLY CONFIDENT.

551
00:23:10,022 --> 00:23:11,423
Adrianne: I THINK SHE'S JUST
VERY USED

552
00:23:11,423 --> 00:23:12,324
TO ALWAYS GETTING HER WAY.

553
00:23:12,324 --> 00:23:13,993
AND WHAT ABOUT EBONY?

554
00:23:13,993 --> 00:23:16,495
Adrianne: EBONY,
YOU BETTER WORK IT, GIRL.

555
00:23:16,495 --> 00:23:18,664
I NEED SOME MOISTURIZER,
SHE WAS COOL.

556
00:23:18,664 --> 00:23:21,200
SHE TOLD ME I DIDN'T UNDERSTAND
HER ESSENCE.

557
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,468
THE ESSENCE.

558
00:23:22,468 --> 00:23:24,737
EVEN THOUGH GISELLE COULD BE
ANNOYING SOMETIMES,

559
00:23:24,737 --> 00:23:27,973
WHEN SHE WASN'T,
SHE WAS ACTUALLY COOL.

560
00:23:27,973 --> 00:23:31,043
WHEN KESSE LEFT, I FELT LIKE
DOWN

561
00:23:31,043 --> 00:23:32,678
JUST BECAUSE I LIKED HER A LOT.

562
00:23:32,678 --> 00:23:34,313
Shannon: JUST HAD, LIKE, THIS
FREE PERSONALITY.

563
00:23:34,313 --> 00:23:36,081
LIKE, REALLY, WHAT LIT HER UP
WAS, LIKE, GOING OUT DANCING

564
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:37,616
OR GOING OUT TO EAT.

565
00:23:37,616 --> 00:23:40,185
SHE JUST, LIKE,
TOTALLY SPARKED UP.

566
00:23:40,185 --> 00:23:43,656
Adrianne: BUT THE ONE THAT I
REALLY HONESTLY DID NOT LIKE

567
00:23:43,656 --> 00:23:46,625
WAS SOMEONE WHO I THOUGHT WAS
VERY, VERY, VERY FAKE

568
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:49,428
WHEN I FINALLY FOUND OUT WHO
THEY WERE, AND THAT WAS ROBIN.

569
00:23:49,428 --> 00:23:52,698
SHE WAS AWFUL TO ME AT THE END.

570
00:23:52,698 --> 00:23:55,167
AS OPPOSED WITH HER, WHO
BELIEVES IN GOD AND STUFF

571
00:23:55,167 --> 00:23:57,636
AND ACTUALLY ACTS LIKE A DECENT
HUMAN BEING.

572
00:24:00,372 --> 00:24:02,041
I WANNA SEE SOME WALKIN',

573
00:24:02,041 --> 00:24:04,076
AND I'M GONNA DO SOME DOUBLES
WITH Y'ALL.

574
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:09,615
♪♪

575
00:24:19,091 --> 00:24:23,195
Tyra: WHOO!

576
00:24:23,195 --> 00:24:28,500
WHOO!

577
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:31,437
ALL RIGHT, Y'ALL, LET'S DO WHAT
THE SACRAMENTO KINGS DO.

578
00:24:31,437 --> 00:24:32,972
OKAY, YOU GOTTA GO, UHH!

579
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:34,273
YOUR LIVES ARE GONNA BE CHANGED
FOREVER TOMORROW.

580
00:24:34,273 --> 00:24:35,407
UHH!

581
00:24:35,407 --> 00:24:36,141
(laughing)

582
00:24:40,679 --> 00:24:43,215
SHOOT, MAN, I'M STUFFED,
I HAD SO MUCH FOOD.

583
00:24:43,215 --> 00:24:44,616
(Adrianne belches)

584
00:24:44,616 --> 00:24:46,552
I REALLY ADMIRE THAT SHE DOESN'T
CARE WHAT ANYONE THINKS OF HER.

585
00:24:46,552 --> 00:24:48,020
SHE'S HERSELF NO MATTER WHAT.

586
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,121
LOOK AT THAT ZIT.

587
00:24:49,121 --> 00:24:50,656
THAT ZIT NEEDS TO GO BEFORE
TOMORROW.

588
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:52,558
THAT'S A BIG WHOPPER.

589
00:24:52,558 --> 00:24:53,559
Shannon: POP IT.

590
00:24:53,559 --> 00:24:54,994
Adrianne: EW!

591
00:24:54,994 --> 00:24:55,494
Shannon: YOU WANT ME TO POP IT
FOR YA?

592
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:56,528
Adrianne: NO.

593
00:24:56,528 --> 00:24:57,696
Shannon: I SWEAR IT'LL GO DOWN.

594
00:24:57,696 --> 00:24:59,231
Adrianne: IT'S PAINFUL.

595
00:24:59,231 --> 00:25:00,332
Shannon: I'LL POP IT.

596
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:01,300
Adrianne: NO!

597
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:02,401
Shannon: PLEASE?

598
00:25:02,401 --> 00:25:04,203
Adrianne: DON'T, GROSS.

599
00:25:04,203 --> 00:25:07,573
I'VE REALLY ENJOYED OUR PAST
COUPLE OF DAYS TOGETHER.

600
00:25:07,573 --> 00:25:10,442
WE'RE COMPLETE OPPOSITES, BUT AT
LEAST SHE DOESN'T MAKE ME

601
00:25:10,442 --> 00:25:13,245
FEEL LIKE -- FOR BEING WHO I AM.

602
00:25:13,245 --> 00:25:15,347
GOOD NIGHT, SHANNON.

603
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:17,383
Shannon: GOOD NIGHT.

604
00:25:17,383 --> 00:25:19,084
'CAUSE TOMORROW WE FIGHT TO THE
DEATH.

605
00:25:19,084 --> 00:25:23,989
♪♪

606
00:25:28,994 --> 00:25:31,563
Kimora: SO YOU'RE HERE TODAY TO
DO A FITTING

607
00:25:31,563 --> 00:25:36,168
FOR THE SHOW THAT'S TONIGHT, AND
IT'S A HIGH RUNWAY, LONG RUNWAY,

608
00:25:36,168 --> 00:25:39,738
LOUD MUSIC, LOTS OF PEOPLE,
POLITICIANS, MUSICIANS,

609
00:25:39,738 --> 00:25:42,341
RAPPERS, ROCKERS, EVERYTHING.

610
00:25:42,341 --> 00:25:43,976
SO... READY?

611
00:25:43,976 --> 00:25:44,510
YES.

612
00:25:48,013 --> 00:25:49,114
Kimora: IS THIS SNUG ON YOU?

613
00:25:49,114 --> 00:25:50,249
Adrianne: MMM.

614
00:25:50,249 --> 00:25:52,651
THESE THINGS LOOK VERY FULL ON
YOU.

615
00:25:52,651 --> 00:25:54,253
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT THAT.

616
00:25:54,253 --> 00:25:55,287
Kimora: YOU'RE VERY THIN.

617
00:25:55,287 --> 00:25:56,722
Shannon: YEAH.

618
00:25:56,722 --> 00:25:59,091
NOW I GUESS YOU HAVE TO DO A
LITTLE HAIR, A LITTLE MAKEUP,

619
00:25:59,091 --> 00:26:01,293
AND I'LL SEE YOU BACK AT THE
SPOT IN A LITTLE WHILE.

620
00:26:01,293 --> 00:26:02,461
Shannon: OKAY.

621
00:26:02,461 --> 00:26:05,998
♪♪

622
00:26:18,110 --> 00:26:21,480
Adrianne: I'M A LITTLE NERVOUS,
BUT I'VE GONE SO FAR.

623
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:25,117
I'VE DONE SO MUCH HERE, AND I
WOULDN'T TRADE THIS EXPERIENCE

624
00:26:25,117 --> 00:26:28,420
FOR ANYTHING IN THE WORLD.

625
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:30,022
Shannon: IT'S JUST VERY,
VERY NERVE-RACKING.

626
00:26:30,022 --> 00:26:30,556
I'M SO NERVOUS, I HAVE GOOSE
BUMPS RIGHT NOW.

627
00:26:33,292 --> 00:26:35,527
WHEN WE FIRST ARRIVED, WE WALKED
IN, AND WE HAD, LIKE, YOU KNOW,

628
00:26:35,527 --> 00:26:38,497
PASSES AROUND OUR NECK, AND THAT
JUST MAKES YOU FEEL COOL.

629
00:26:41,733 --> 00:26:45,070
THE ENERGY WAS VERY FAST-PACED,
VERY HECTIC.

630
00:26:45,070 --> 00:26:46,305
Tyra: SEE, YOUR MAKEUP LOOKS
GORGEOUS.

631
00:26:46,305 --> 00:26:48,474
Shannon: YOU GOT, LIKE, PEOPLE
DOING MY MAKEUP, AND IT WAS

632
00:26:48,474 --> 00:26:51,009
JUST, LIKE, YOU KNOW, FAST,
BUT I ENJOYED IT.

633
00:26:51,009 --> 00:26:54,079
Tyra: REMEMBER, CHIN DOWN.

634
00:26:54,079 --> 00:26:55,147
RELAX THE SHOULDERS.

635
00:26:55,147 --> 00:26:58,016
Adrianne: YEAH, RELAX THE
SHOULDERS.

636
00:26:58,016 --> 00:26:59,751
Tyra: I'LL BE YELLING AT YOU ON
THE RUNWAY FOR DOING IT, OKAY?

637
00:26:59,751 --> 00:27:02,554
Shannon: I WON'T.
Tyra: ALL RIGHT.

638
00:27:02,554 --> 00:27:04,123
Adrianne: I DON'T
LIKE TO BE NERVOUS.

639
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:06,492
I WANNA BUST MY BALLS AND GET
THIS.

640
00:27:06,492 --> 00:27:09,995
BEFORE WE WENT ON, I PEERED OUT
IN THE BIG TENT,

641
00:27:09,995 --> 00:27:11,663
WHICH THE SHOW WAS HELD.

642
00:27:11,663 --> 00:27:12,664
IT WAS AWESOME.

643
00:27:12,664 --> 00:27:14,766
THERE WAS A LOT OF PEOPLE.

644
00:27:14,766 --> 00:27:16,602
Tyra: THERE'S NO RETOUCHING ON
THE RUNWAY.

645
00:27:16,602 --> 00:27:18,570
THERE'S NO ROOM FOR MISTAKES.

646
00:27:18,570 --> 00:27:20,405
HOPEFULLY, IT WAS FIERCE.

647
00:27:20,405 --> 00:27:22,441
HOPEFULLY, IT WAS PERFECT.

648
00:27:22,441 --> 00:27:27,279
AND IF IT WASN'T, THE WHOLE ROOM
AND THE WHOLE WORLD

649
00:27:27,279 --> 00:27:30,249
JUST SAW YOU SCREW UP.

650
00:27:30,249 --> 00:27:34,286
♪♪

651
00:27:43,695 --> 00:27:45,197
(applause)

652
00:27:45,197 --> 00:27:48,000
WHOO!

653
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,402
BEING ON THAT STAGE WITH THOSE
LIGHTS-- OH!

654
00:27:50,402 --> 00:27:52,070
IT JUST, LIKE, TRANSFORMED ME.

655
00:27:52,070 --> 00:27:53,972
LIKE, I WAS ON CLOUD NINE.

656
00:27:53,972 --> 00:27:55,741
♪ NEVER DOUBT NO DOUBT
WHAT IT IS WHERE IT'S AT ♪

657
00:27:55,741 --> 00:27:57,676
♪ WHAT IT'S ABOUT TRUDGING
THROUGH THE UNDERGROUND ♪

658
00:27:57,676 --> 00:27:59,344
♪ NO ONE'S HERE
TO MAP IT ALL OUT ♪

659
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:01,380
♪ BEFORE YOU BLACK OUT
PULLING YOU OUT OF THE MIST ♪

660
